     "type": "intro",
     "title": "From Slave to Sage",
     "content": "Epictetus (c. 50–135 CE) began life enslaved in Hierapolis (modern Turkey) and ended it as the most influential Stoic teacher of the Roman Empire. The Enchiridion — Greek for 'handbook' or 'something held in the hand' — distills his teaching into 53 short chapters meant to be carried like a sword in battle. This seminar reads the Enchiridion as a practical curriculum for living well.",
